    "body": "Diagnosis from a macOS worker. No claim was made and no code was changed.\n\n- Cause: the test builds the expected path as `base.join(\".cargo/config.toml\")` at `xtask/src/unit_env/config.rs:139` on upstream/main `1cf7390dc0ac`.\n- On Windows, this path keeps the `/` separator. `notes()` builds the path with `parent.join(\".cargo\")` and then `join(\"config.toml\")`, so it prints `\\`.\n- Thus `line.contains(&path)` finds no line, and `expect(\"fixture config warning\")` fails.\n- The runtime diagnostic is correct. Only the expected path in the test is wrong.\n- Proposed fix: `base.join(\".cargo\").join(\"config.toml\")` (one line). This is the same correction as PR #4449 for #4426, which is merged.\n- The sibling #4427 has the same cause: it asserts `contains(\"home/config.toml\")`. A native-separator form is `Path::new(\"home\").join(\"config.toml\")`.\n\nI stopped because I cannot show the pin fail on macOS. On macOS, `/` is the native separator, so the test passes before and after the change. A worker on a Windows host must show the red result before the fix.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
